  "cameraLip": {
    "instrument": "Legacy head camera, same for every viseme. PerspectiveCamera fov 35, aspect 1280/960, near 0.01, far 50. Position 0.5297281360924244, 1.68536235332489, 0.8719936575591564. lookAt 0.0017281360924243927, 1.5586723208427429, 0.05599365755915642. The camera looks down its -Z, so a larger camera-space z is closer. Samples are rest-pose arch-face vertices (round 2 mm x bins, verts within 2 mm of that bin's rest max z, row clear of the teeth Y median by 0.006 m) plus posed edge midpoints of face-array neighbors within 7 slots and 2.5 mm. A sample is in front when its camera z exceeds the closest body vertex within 6 px, among body verts with world y in [1.43, 1.56] and |x| <= 0.06 that project inside 1280x960. Buckets are inclusive: 0.2–2 mm, 2–8 mm, and more than 8 mm. The 0.2–2 mm bucket is the lip cut. The >8 mm bucket is teeth in the opening in front of the throat.",
